---
date: 2026-07-29T23:41:12-04:00
---

Giant is a towering creature, even by the standards of the would-be-gods around it. Clad in red monk’s robes, half tied shut by a golden cord that must be as large as a building. Clouds gather around its chest, obscuring the view of its face beyond, but peeking out over the cover are two horns: one ground to a flat base, and the other sharpened to a wicked edge.

A likeness of Giant trampling a crowd stands on one of the six god doors in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]]. Behind the door is the plant where [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] built radar dishes and prepared for the pilgrimage.

On the far side of the fracture beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], a Giant figure stands in a wide river with its feet in the water and its shoulders above the cloud line, and does not move. The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] compound two miles off watches it.

[[Aut]] says the Giant is stuck behind the [[Firmament|firmament]] at the far starward end of the horizon, held there by whoever made the firmament, and that it has beaten against the wall for years with nothing to show for it. He visits it to laugh. He says the [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Judge of Ages|Judge]] could likely beat the Giant one to one, but gods of their kind never fight one to one.
